r"""patch_L477_2_drawer_view_build_20261024.py

The build of Tony's four rulings of October 24, 2026 on his Oct 23 phone
look, in the gallery (website) repository. Ledger L-477 to L-480; the
design record is documentation/DESIGN_L477_drawer_and_view_rulings_20261024.md
in the orrery.

Built on gallery 2c2057d7f11794fe5c2805af955dbc452519c644 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io and orrery
82fa04cc634c58544b9a2bb4aeb57310a2000515 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery

HOW TO RUN: save this file in the gallery folder,
C:\Users\tonyq\OneDrive\Desktop\python_work\tonyquintanilla.github.io\
open it in VS Code and click Run (the same as: python
patch_L477_2_drawer_view_build_20261024.py). It asks nothing. Then run
gallery_maintenance_run.py, move this file to documentation/, commit and
push. After the push: gallery_maintenance_run.py --live, then the phone
look. No cache rebuild is needed: every change reaches a visitor on the
push alone.

What it changes, all or nothing:
  - interactive.html: the Solar System room's drawer has no See more and
    no "All". Every group is listed, folded shut; a group row only folds,
    with its arrow where a body has its box. The top bar's button reads
    Reset there and puts back what the room opened on, every group folded
    shut, the opening frame and angle. Inside an open group, once one of
    its bodies is ticked, "Reset <group>" unticks them (L-477). The count
    line moves to the lower left, above the drawer's handle, out of the
    HUD on the right (L-478). Go To fits the body's whole orbit and opens
    its text box; a tick still frames on where bodies are now; and every
    body's hover ends with "Orbit: q to Q AU from the Sun." (L-479). The
    room's i panel words follow. The Sun and Earth rooms are unchanged:
    their drawers and All / none are as before.
  - gallery/solar_system_drawer.js: the drawer's logic, as above.
  - gallery/solar_system_figures.js: orbitLine, the orbit's near and far
    distance from the served a and e, three figures, never finer than the
    body's distance error earns.
  - data/objects_config.json: the six group rows lose "see_more", and the
    rows' explanation says what the drawer now does.
  - index.html: closing the About card that a room's i panel opened steps
    back to the room (L-480).
  - documentation/smoke_solar_system_drawer.js and
    documentation/smoke_solar_system_figures.js: the checks, with seven
    and three planted faults; tools/headless/walk_solar_system_drawer.js,
    the headless walk (Claude-only).

Success: one "ok" line per file, then "patch applied". Failure: one
"ERROR:" or "ANCHOR FAIL" line and NOTHING is written. A second run
refuses. If something looks wrong after a run, Discard Changes in GitHub
Desktop undoes it.

Written October 24, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
